    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "＊A tricky piece of grammar. The meaning in Japanese is as follows:\n〜ときは、いつも\n〜ときも、ときも\n\n＊「Ａにつけ、Ｂにつけ」 is a common construction. A and B are often pairs or two of a kind, such as strong/weak, good/evil, etc.\n\nFORMATION:\nＶ(plain form) + につけ\nいＡ + につけ",
      "html": "＊A tricky piece of grammar. The meaning in Japanese is as follows:<br/>〜ときは、いつも<br/>〜ときも、ときも<br/><br/>＊「Ａにつけ、Ｂにつけ」 is a common construction. A and B are often pairs or two of a kind, such as strong/weak, good/evil, etc.<br/><br/>FORMATION:<br/>Ｖ(plain form) + につけ<br/>いＡ + につけ",
      "credits_raw": "rubyhatchet",
      "content_sha256": "2dfd7186a127f322a26ee721433c74e5a782be92e2f395f32eb62a2ad219c366",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Hmm... what's the difference between nitsuke and tabini?",
      "html": "Hmm... what's the difference between nitsuke and tabini?",
      "credits_raw": "Darrkangel",
      "content_sha256": "143cff1d4dfb132ada73b86b2d72add1c32759f6b73d9c58bcf3beed13cb5c6d",
